---
import { CLOSING_RULE } from '../lib/site';
interface Props { dateLabel?: string | null; variant?: 'law' | 'guide' | 'record' | 'company' }
const { dateLabel, variant = 'law' } = Astro.props;
---
<aside class="box box--ink" aria-labelledby="before-you-rely" id="before-you-rely-box">
  <p class="band__title" id="before-you-rely">Before you rely on this</p>
  <ul class="prose">
    {variant === 'company' ? (
      <>
        <li>Contact details, hours, and the list of services on this page came from the company itself. We have not watched any of that work being done, and we do not repeat it as fact.</li>
        <li>Certifications and guild membership came from an issuer's own public roster, on the dates shown on this page. A roster entry is a subscription or a test somebody passed on a day — not a guarantee of competence, honesty, or insurance.</li>
        <li>A page here is not an endorsement, a recommendation, or an approval. No company can pay to appear on this site, to rank higher on it, or to be left off it. Placement is never sold, at any price.</li>
        <li>Hiring is your decision. Ask for a dated certificate of liability insurance, ask which NFPA 211 inspection level you are buying, and get the findings in writing before money changes hands.</li>
      </>
    ) : variant === 'record' ? (
      <>
        <li>A record is not an endorsement, a recommendation, or an approval. Appearing here means a certification number was searched for on an issuer's own roster — nothing else, and nobody is vouched for.</li>
        <li>A certification is not a guarantee of competence or honesty. It is a test somebody passed on a day, recorded by the body that set it.</li>
        <li>Facts go stale. Certifications lapse, people change employers, and rosters are corrected without telling us.</li>
        <li>Hiring is your decision. Ask for the certificate, check the issuer's roster yourself, and get a written inspection report before money changes hands.</li>
      </>
    ) : variant === 'law' ? (
      <>
        <li>This is not legal advice. For a dispute, talk to a lawyer licensed in your state or your state attorney general's consumer office.</li>
        <li>Laws change. Statutes, thresholds and code editions can move after we look.</li>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <li>This is general information, not professional advice. What a qualified technician finds in your chimney — shown to you, in writing — outranks any guide.</li>
        <li>Standards change. NFPA 211 and the IRC are revised on a cycle, and your local building department decides which edition applies to your home.</li>
        <li>Price ranges are researched national figures, not quotes. Your region, roof and chimney condition move the real number.</li>
        <li>State rules differ. For licensing, permits and home-sale rules, read the <a href="/rights">50-state laws table</a>.</li>
      </>
    )}
    <li>Every date on this page is only when we last looked{dateLabel ? ` (${dateLabel})` : ''} — not a promise that nothing has changed since.</li>
    <li>{CLOSING_RULE}</li>
  </ul>
</aside>
